<h2>1. Jasper — Best for Marketing Copy at Scale</h2>
<p><strong>Rating: 4.6/5</strong></p>
<p>Jasper is the one tool on this list built specifically for marketers rather than adapted from a general chatbot. The current product is organised around agents for recurring marketing jobs — campaign briefs, product descriptions, ad variants — layered on top of a brand-voice system that constrains tone and format. Pro includes two brand voices, five knowledge assets and three audiences; Business removes those caps and adds the no-code agent builder.</p>
<p><strong>Pricing:</strong> Pro $69/mo ($59/mo billed yearly) · Business custom. Pro includes a 7-day free trial.</p>
<p><strong>Free tier:</strong> No permanent free plan — a 7-day trial on Pro.</p>
<p><strong>Who it's for:</strong> Teams producing copy across many surfaces who need the output to sound like one brand. <strong>Not for:</strong> solo operators writing two blog posts a month — a general assistant covers that at a fraction of the cost.</p>
<p class="flex items-center gap-2 flex-wrap">
  <a href="/tool/jasper" class="btn-primary">See Jasper in the directory →</a>
</p>

<h2>2. Surfer — Best for Content That Ranks and Gets Cited</h2>
<p><strong>Rating: 4.3/5</strong></p>
<p>Surfer has repositioned from a content optimiser into an AI-search visibility platform, which is the more useful framing in 2026: the question is no longer only whether a page ranks in Google, but whether ChatGPT, Perplexity and AI Overviews mention your brand at all. The content side still works the way it always did — draft in the editor, get scored against the live SERP structure, fix the gaps — and the AI Search Analytics tier adds brand-mention tracking across five models.</p>
<p><strong>Pricing:</strong> Discovery $49/mo · Standard $99/mo · Pro $182/mo · Peace of Mind $299/mo. Discovery covers 120 documents and 10 tracked pages; Standard adds AI-visibility tracking on ChatGPT with 25 prompts refreshed weekly.</p>
<p><strong>Free tier:</strong> None — paid plans only.</p>
<p><strong>Who it's for:</strong> Content teams whose growth depends on organic and AI-search visibility. <strong>Not for:</strong> teams that need broad competitive intelligence — that is Semrush's job.</p>
<p class="flex items-center gap-2 flex-wrap">
  <a href="/tool/surfer-seo" class="btn-primary">See Surfer in the directory →</a>
</p>

<h2>3. Semrush — Best for Research and Competitive Analysis</h2>
<p><strong>Rating: 4.5/5</strong></p>
<p>Semrush remains the widest toolkit in the category: keyword research, position tracking, site audit, backlinks, PPC intelligence and now AI-visibility reporting in the same subscription. The SEO plan tracks five websites and 500 keywords daily; the tiers above it add prompt tracking across ChatGPT, Perplexity, Gemini and AI Overviews, plus historical data.</p>
<p><strong>Pricing:</strong> Free ($0, 1 demo project, 10 reports/day) · SEO $139/mo ($117.33/mo billed yearly) · Starter $199/mo ($165.17/mo yearly) · Pro+ $299/mo ($248.17/mo yearly) · Advanced custom.</p>
<p><strong>Free tier:</strong> Yes — a demo project and 10 reports a day, useful for a one-off check rather than ongoing work.</p>
<p><strong>Who it's for:</strong> Teams that need one source of truth for search data. <strong>Not for:</strong> writers who only need to optimise a draft — that is Surfer, and it costs less.</p>
<p class="flex items-center gap-2 flex-wrap">
  <a href="/tool/semrush" class="btn-primary">See Semrush in the directory →</a>
</p>

<h2>4. Synthesia — Best for Avatar Video and Localisation</h2>
<p><strong>Rating: 4.5/5</strong></p>
<p>For marketing teams, Synthesia's value is not novelty — it is producing the same video in eight languages without reshooting anything. Script-to-avatar video covers product explainers, onboarding sequences and ad variants, and the platform ships SOC 2 Type II and ISO 27001 certification, which is usually what gets it past procurement rather than the avatar quality.</p>
<p><strong>Pricing:</strong> Free Basic (10 min/mo, watermarked, 9 avatars) · Starter $19/mo ($14/mo billed yearly, $168/yr — 1,250 credits, 125+ avatars) · Pro $89/mo ($59/mo billed yearly, 6,000 credits, 180+ avatars, 5 personal avatars) · Enterprise custom.</p>
<p><strong>Free tier:</strong> Yes — about 10 minutes of video a month, watermarked.</p>
<p><strong>Who it's for:</strong> Teams producing explainers, training and localised campaigns at volume. <strong>Not for:</strong> brand films that need cinematic production value.</p>
<p class="flex items-center gap-2 flex-wrap">
  <AffiliateBtn slug="synthesia" text="Start Free with Synthesia" loc="marketers-listicle" />
  <a href="/synthesia-review" class="text-sm font-medium text-[#3B82F6] hover:underline">Read the full Synthesia review →</a>
</p>

<h2>5. ElevenLabs — Best for Voiceover and Audio Ads</h2>
<p><strong>Rating: 4.7/5</strong></p>
<p>Voice is the cheapest part of a video production budget to automate and the most obvious when it is wrong. ElevenLabs covers narration, voice cloning from short samples and dubbing, with language coverage that depends on the TTS model: {ELEVENLABS_LANGS.inline}. For marketers the practical uses are audio ads, video narration at volume and re-voicing existing creative for new markets.</p>
<p><strong>Pricing:</strong> Free (10,000 credits/mo) · Starter $6/mo (30,000 credits) · Creator $22/mo (121,000 credits, professional voice cloning) · Pro $99/mo · Scale $299/mo · Business $990/mo.</p>
<p><strong>Free tier:</strong> Yes — 10,000 characters a month, roughly ten minutes of finished speech.</p>
<p><strong>Who it's for:</strong> Anyone producing narrated video or audio at volume. <strong>Not for:</strong> live broadcast work — the licensing and latency story is different there.</p>
<p class="flex items-center gap-2 flex-wrap">
  <AffiliateBtn slug="elevenlabs" text="Start Free on ElevenLabs" loc="marketers-listicle" />
  <a href="/elevenlabs-review" class="text-sm font-medium text-[#3B82F6] hover:underline">Read the full ElevenLabs review →</a>
</p>

<h2>6. Submagic — Best for Turning Webinars Into Short-Form</h2>
<p><strong>Rating: 4.5/5</strong></p>
<p>Most B2B marketing teams already sit on hours of webinar and interview footage that never becomes social content because nothing gets cut. Submagic handles the repetitive part: transcription, animated captions, silence and bad-take removal, and Magic Clips that propose vertical cuts from a long recording. It is not an editor for creative control — it is a volume tool.</p>
<p><strong>Pricing:</strong> Starter $19/mo ($12/mo billed yearly — 45 credits, about 15 captioned videos or 5 Magic Clips) · Pro $39/mo ($23/mo yearly) · Business $69/mo ($41/mo yearly) · Custom.</p>
<p><strong>Free tier:</strong> No permanent free plan — a trial covering a handful of videos, no credit card required.</p>
<p><strong>Who it's for:</strong> Teams with a content archive and a posting cadence to feed. <strong>Not for:</strong> teams that need frame-level editing.</p>
<p class="flex items-center gap-2 flex-wrap">
  <AffiliateBtn slug="submagic" text="Start Free Trial" loc="marketers-listicle" />
  <a href="/submagic-review" class="text-sm font-medium text-[#3B82F6] hover:underline">Read the full Submagic review →</a>
</p>

<h2>7. Canva — Best for Creative Assets Without a Designer Queue</h2>
<p><strong>Rating: 4.6/5</strong></p>
<p>Canva's role in a marketing stack is volume with brand consistency: social templates, ad variants, lead magnets, event collateral. The free tier covers 1.6M+ templates and a single brand kit; paid tiers add brand kits at scale, approvals, social scheduling and a much larger AI allowance. For teams already paying for a designer, Canva is the tool that removes the small-request queue.</p>
<p><strong>Pricing:</strong> Free · Pro and Business billed annually or monthly. Pro is the single-user tier; Business adds team admin, approvals and more AI allowance per seat.</p>
<p><strong>Free tier:</strong> Yes — genuinely usable for social and presentation work.</p>
<p><strong>Who it's for:</strong> Marketers shipping dozens of assets a week. <strong>Not for:</strong> work that needs print-grade production control.</p>
<p class="flex items-center gap-2 flex-wrap">
  <a href="/tool/canva" class="btn-primary">See Canva in the directory →</a>
</p>

<h2>8. HubSpot — Best for CRM and Email Automation</h2>
<p><strong>Rating: 4.4/5</strong></p>
<p>HubSpot is the only tool here that is a system of record rather than a utility. The free tier gives two users a CRM, forms and basic email; Starter adds credits, Agent Hub and ad management; Professional is where automation, social and video tooling arrive — including AEO, which tracks how your brand appears in ChatGPT, Gemini and Perplexity.</p>
<p><strong>Pricing:</strong> Free $0 · Starter $20/mo/seat (frequently discounted) · Professional $890/mo monthly ($800/mo billed annually, plus a one-time $3,000 onboarding fee) · Enterprise $3,600/mo (plus $7,000 onboarding). The AEO add-on alone is $50/mo ($45/mo annually) and is included in Professional and above.</p>
<p><strong>Free tier:</strong> Yes — two users, no credit card.</p>
<p><strong>Who it's for:</strong> Teams that need marketing and sales in one database. <strong>Not for:</strong> teams who only need a sending tool — the Professional jump and onboarding fee are hard to justify below that scale.</p>
<p class="flex items-center gap-2 flex-wrap">
  <a href="/tool/hubspot-ai" class="btn-primary">See HubSpot in the directory →</a>
</p>

<h2>9. Zapier — Best for Gluing the Stack Together</h2>
<p><strong>Rating: 4.5/5</strong></p>
<p>Every tool above has an export and an import, and none of them natively agree on what a lead is. Zapier is the boring infrastructure that makes the rest of the stack behave like one system: form submission into CRM, new content into a review queue, campaign data into a reporting sheet. The free tier covers simple two-step automations; paid tiers add multi-step workflows and more task volume.</p>
<p><strong>Pricing:</strong> Free (100 tasks/mo, two-step Zaps) · paid plans from $19.99/mo, scaling by task volume rather than seats.</p>
<p><strong>Free tier:</strong> Yes — 100 tasks a month, enough to validate a workflow before paying.</p>
<p><strong>Who it's for:</strong> Anyone running three or more tools that need to share data. <strong>Not for:</strong> teams already on a platform where the integrations are built in.</p>
<p class="flex items-center gap-2 flex-wrap">
  <a href="/tool/zapier" class="btn-primary">See Zapier in the directory →</a>
</p>

